<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer - key that EU saw long-term stability need.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer - key that EU saw long-term stability need.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer on Thursday said that it was of major importance that the European Union had seen the need for long-term budget stability rather than for one-off beneficial measures.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference Tietmeyer pointed to the requirement of the Maastricht Treaty for the single European currency for &quot;very clear lasting, enduring adherance&quot; to the budgetary criteria.</p>
<p>Referring to the criteria, he noted that the 60 percent debt-to-GDP limit was just as valid as the public deficit-GDP limit of three percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
